SELECT 'Freshdesk Freddy', 'freshdesk.com', 'compliant_with_caveats', '"By using the AI Services, unless Customer opts-out as further set forth below and in the Documentation Customer grants Freshworks a royalty-free license to use its Customer Data and AI Output for AI Training and expressly consents to such AI Training." "Customers who wish to opt out of their Customer Data being used to train both Collaborative Models and Custom Models may do so by contacting support@freshworks.com and indicating they wish to opt out of all AI Training." Training is on by default once a business uses Freshworks'' AI Services (Freddy AI in Freshdesk). Section 4(d) of the Supplemental Terms gives two opt-out levels, both by emailing support@freshworks.com: “Opt Out of Training Collaborative Models”, which keeps the AI Services working, possibly with reduced performance, or “Opt Out of All AI Training”, which covers both Collaborative and Custom Models. Freshworks says training stops within seven business days of the opt-out notice, and its training licence expires 180 days after the business terminates the AI Services or opts out. Only the business that holds the Freshworks account can opt out; end users and people who contact a company''s Freshdesk helpdesk can''t opt out themselves. The Supplemental Terms also say Freshworks will not use or permit customer data to train third-party hosted generative AI models. Where Freshworks'' Freddy AI FAQ describes the opt-out differently, the Supplemental Terms take precedence. Source: Freshworks Supplemental Terms (Effective Date March 6, 2026), checked 17 November 2026; Freshworks'' legal pages cover Freshdesk.', NULL, 1, NULL, '["https://www.freshworks.com/terms/supplemental-terms/"]', 1, 0, 0, '2026-11-17T09:42:00.000Z', 1, 1, 0
